  "description": "The failure ladder of 0300-DALYREJS-OPEN :292-306, reached before a single transaction is read. The OPEN OUTPUT at :293 is arranged to report a status other than '00', so :297 moves 12 into APPL-RESULT and :302-305 display 'ERROR OPENING DALY REJECTS FILE', render the status and abend. The seeded input is case01's, which would have posted cleanly: that is the point, because it shows the open ladder firing on its own rather than as a consequence of anything the data does. DALYREJS is the fourth of the six opens - :195-200 orders them DALYTRAN, TRANFILE, XREFFILE, DALYREJS, ACCTFILE, TCATBALF - so the two opens after it never happen either, and neither does the loop. RETURN-CODE is 12, there are no count lines and there is no closing banner. A run whose rejects file cannot be established writes nothing anywhere, which is why every dataset comes back exactly as it was seeded.",
